1
00:00:02,720 --> 00:00:04,241
I'm Peppa Pig

2
00:00:04,800 --> 00:00:07,120
and this is my little brother, George

3
00:00:07,513 --> 00:00:09,140
This is Mummy Pig

4
00:00:09,840 --> 00:00:11,283
And this is Daddy Pig

5
00:00:13,562 --> 00:00:14,842
Peppa Pig

6
00:00:19,849 --> 00:00:21,959
"Mr. Scarecrow"

7
00:00:24,124 --> 00:00:25,430
Today, Peppa and George

8
00:00:25,470 --> 00:00:27,350
are visiting Granny and Grandpa Pig

9
00:00:32,023 --> 00:00:34,694
-Hello, Grandpa Pig
-Hello, Grandpa Pig

10
00:00:35,596 --> 00:00:36,634
Hello, Peppa

11
00:00:36,674 --> 00:00:37,958
Hello, George

12
00:00:37,998 --> 00:00:40,439
Grandpa, what are you doing?

13
00:00:40,479 --> 00:00:42,939
I'm working in my garden

14
00:00:44,301 --> 00:00:48,063
These seeds will grow into lovely flowers

15
00:00:48,644 --> 00:00:51,536
All I do is put the seeds in the ground

16
00:00:52,631 --> 00:00:55,471
and then cover the seeds with earth

17
00:00:55,773 --> 00:00:57,853
Oh, where have the seeds gone?

18
00:00:57,973 --> 00:00:59,534
The seeds are gone

19
00:00:59,574 --> 00:01:01,014
That's strange

20
00:01:01,054 --> 00:01:03,615
I'm sure I put the seeds here

21
00:01:03,655 --> 00:01:06,316
Yes, Grandpa, we saw you

22
00:01:06,456 --> 00:01:08,513
But the seeds aren't here now

23
00:01:08,553 --> 00:01:11,886
Never mind, I'll just have to put some more seeds in

24
00:01:12,206 --> 00:01:13,858
As I was saying

25
00:01:13,898 --> 00:01:16,766
all I do is put the seeds in the ground

26
00:01:19,072 --> 00:01:22,156
A bird is eating Grandpa's seeds

27
00:01:23,357 --> 00:01:25,324
You can't eat my seeds!

28
00:01:25,670 --> 00:01:28,217
Now I know where the seeds went

29
00:01:28,257 --> 00:01:30,859
They're inside the bird's tummy

30
00:01:32,581 --> 00:01:35,583
Two more birds have come to eat Grandpa's seeds

31
00:01:35,724 --> 00:01:37,217
Oh, look

32
00:01:37,871 --> 00:01:39,432
Shoo! Shoo!

33
00:01:39,848 --> 00:01:41,634
What's all the noise?

34
00:01:41,729 --> 00:01:42,931
Oh, Granny

35
00:01:42,972 --> 00:01:45,739
The birds have eaten all my flower seeds

36
00:01:45,779 --> 00:01:48,425
So we're shooing the birds away

37
00:01:48,465 --> 00:01:51,633
Shooing them won't work, they'll just come back

38
00:01:51,673 --> 00:01:52,658
Look

39
00:01:53,718 --> 00:01:55,584
We need a scarecrow

40
00:01:55,671 --> 00:01:57,344
What's a scarecrow?

41
00:01:57,385 --> 00:01:59,635
A scarecrow is a man made of straw

42
00:01:59,676 --> 00:02:01,423
that scares the birds away

43
00:02:01,464 --> 00:02:04,223
That's a great idea, Granny

44
00:02:04,371 --> 00:02:05,890
I'll go make one

45
00:02:05,931 --> 00:02:07,573
Follow me

46
00:02:08,522 --> 00:02:10,203
Bye-bye, birds

47
00:02:10,376 --> 00:02:13,013
We're going to make a scarecrow now

48
00:02:15,129 --> 00:02:17,690
This is Grandpa's garden shed

49
00:02:17,872 --> 00:02:21,451
There are lots of things here to make a scarecrow with

50
00:02:21,884 --> 00:02:25,471
First, we need two sticks and some string

51
00:02:25,515 --> 00:02:27,083
Let's find them

52
00:02:30,082 --> 00:02:31,775
Peppa has found some sticks

53
00:02:31,815 --> 00:02:33,456
and George has found some string

54
00:02:33,496 --> 00:02:34,496
Excellent

55
00:02:34,588 --> 00:02:38,038
I'll tie the two sticks together to make the body

56
00:02:38,560 --> 00:02:41,441
Grannny has found some straw and an old sack

57
00:02:41,781 --> 00:02:42,781
Very good

58
00:02:42,821 --> 00:02:45,982
I'll put the straw into the sack to make the head

59
00:02:47,610 --> 00:02:50,465
Now we need to dress the scarecrow

60
00:02:50,787 --> 00:02:52,899
Here's a bag of old clothes

61
00:02:56,142 --> 00:02:57,867
George has found a dress

62
00:02:59,420 --> 00:03:00,982
Silly George

63
00:03:01,022 --> 00:03:04,041
Because Mr. Scarecrow doesn't wear dresses

64
00:03:06,028 --> 00:03:07,762
Peppa has found a coat

65
00:03:08,150 --> 00:03:10,192
Very good, Peppa

66
00:03:11,887 --> 00:03:13,527
George has found a hat

67
00:03:13,567 --> 00:03:15,288
Well done, George

68
00:03:15,713 --> 00:03:18,531
Now Mr. Scarecrow needs a face

69
00:03:18,571 --> 00:03:19,811
That's right

70
00:03:19,892 --> 00:03:22,574
Would you and George like to draw his face?

72
00:03:22,614 --> 00:03:23,997
Yes, please

73
00:03:25,429 --> 00:03:27,750
George has drawn two eyes and a nose

74
00:03:28,858 --> 00:03:30,699
And Peppa has drawn a mouth

75
00:03:30,860 --> 00:03:32,994
That looks lovely

76
00:03:33,035 --> 00:03:35,499
- Mr. Scarecrow is ready
- Hooray!

77
00:03:37,646 --> 00:03:40,454
The birds are looking for Grandpa Pig's flower seeds to eat

78
00:03:40,631 --> 00:03:43,192
Look, the birds are back

79
00:03:43,313 --> 00:03:44,829
Don't worry, Peppa

80
00:03:44,870 --> 00:03:47,356
Mr. Scarecrow will scare them away

81
00:03:52,687 --> 00:03:53,747
It worked!

82
00:03:53,788 --> 00:03:56,158
Mr. Scarecrow scared all the birds away

83
00:03:56,245 --> 00:03:57,678
- Hooray!
- Hooray!

84
00:03:57,846 --> 00:03:58,807
Brilliant

85
00:03:58,847 --> 00:04:01,983
The birds won't eat the flower seeds anymore

86
00:04:03,464 --> 00:04:04,947
Oh, Grandpa Pig

87
00:04:04,987 --> 00:04:07,755
The birds look so sad

88
00:04:07,814 --> 00:04:10,214
Are they? They must be very hungry

89
00:04:10,255 --> 00:04:12,153
That's why I brought this

90
00:04:12,193 --> 00:04:13,954
What is it, Granny Pig?

91
00:04:14,035 --> 00:04:15,916
It's a bird feeder

92
00:04:15,957 --> 00:04:18,879
Grandpa Pig, can you give me some seeds?

93
00:04:23,324 --> 00:04:25,927
Come along, birds, lunch is ready

94
00:04:27,738 --> 00:04:30,092
Now the birds have their own seeds to eat

95
00:04:30,132 --> 00:04:31,227
Hooray!

96
00:04:31,268 --> 00:04:33,619
Now the birds are happy again

97
00:04:33,846 --> 00:04:35,025
Peppa is very happy

98
00:04:35,065 --> 00:04:37,710
that Grandpa Pig's seeds weren't eaten by the birds

99
00:04:37,770 --> 00:04:39,236
But she is even happier

100
00:04:39,276 --> 00:04:41,239
that the birds won't be hungry anymore
